B. Create Components and Versions
Step 1: Open Components
1. Open your project.
2. Click ••• (More actions) next to the project name in the sidebar.
3. Select Space settings or View space settings.
4. Click Components.
If Components is not visible in the settings menu, you may need to add it to the project navigation or get administrator access. 
Atlassian Support

Step 2: Create components
1. Click Create component.
2. Enter these example values:
Field	Value
Name	Frontend
Description	User interface development

3. Leave Component lead and Default assignee unchanged if you do not need to set them.
4. Click Save.
Repeat the same steps to create two more components:
Name	Description
Backend	Server-side development
Database	Database-related work

You should now see three components: Frontend, Backend, and Database.
Step 3: Open Versions
1. Stay in your project.
2. Click ••• (More actions) next to the project name.
3. Open Space settings.
4. Select Versions.
In some Jira layouts, this may be shown as Releases instead. If you cannot find either option, open Features in Space settings and enable Releases, if available. 
Atlassian Support+1

Step 4: Create a version
1. Click Create version.
2. Enter the following example values:
Field	Value
Name	Version 1.0
Start date	Leave blank if optional
Release date	Leave blank if optional
Description	First project release

3. Click Save.
Step 5: Create a second version
Repeat Step 4 with these values:
Field	Value
Name	Version 2.0
Description	Second project release

Click Save.
